; Dependency spec for the @duplicates-preserve --extern-import fixture (phase 2). Its minted
; extern-interface export MUST carry the `@duplicates preserve` directive on each table rule so a
; consumer regenerating from the export rebuilds the SAME pair-map twins (PairMap /
; NonEmptyPairMap) — without the projected directive the consumer would rebuild a reject-default
; BTreeMap that silently REJECTS the duplicate keys the dep preserves (the cross-crate skew the seam
; kills, the mirror of the reject direction). Exercises both the `{*}` (PairMap) and `{+}`
; (NonEmptyPairMap) flavors, plus the TAGGED flavor, which force-wraps into a nominal wrapper
; owning its tag: that one projects as an opaque extern type (its codec is its own, exactly like the
; non-preserve tagged-table twin), so what the consumer must NOT do is rebuild a transparent
; pair-map alias whose standalone codec would drop the tag.
preserve_map  = {* uint => text} ; @duplicates preserve
preserve_nmap = {+ uint => text} ; @duplicates preserve
tagged_preserve_map = #6.24({* uint => text}) ; @duplicates preserve
